  "Id": 2743,
  "Title": "ISMC alumna joins BA Research Project in Gilgit",
  "NewsSubTitle": null,
  "NewsSummary": "Scaling Up and Transferring Community-Managed Rural Water Systems to Urban Settings",
  "GlobalNews": false,
  "AlternateNewsTitle": null,
  "AlternateNewsSubtitle": null,
  "AlternateNewsSummary": null,
  "NewsContent": "<div class=\"ExternalClass36A6C3E06C644999ABFDB1C64459A901\"><p>\u200b<br></p><p></p><p>ISMC alumna, Fatima Islam, has joined the Institute\u2019s British Academy funded programme in Gilgit, Pakistan as a Research Assistant.\u200b<br></p><p>Reflecting on how MA in Muslim Cultures helped her prepare for the role she said&#58;&#160;\u201cThe course provided me with the opportunity to understand, critique and engage in an intellectually stimulating way on subjects like world-history and Muslim societies and civilisations. More importantly, it opened new spheres of opportunities for me. This opportunity as a Research Assistant has given me a chance to serve back the community.&#160;I will be involved in the analysis of data for the project, which will be a great way for me to showcase the skills I have honed through the programme whilst providing me an opportunity to develop my research and analytical skills!\u201d\u200b<br><br></p></div>",
